   DOI: 10.1016/j.media.2017.07.005. PMID: 28778026.
   Institution: Radboud University Medical Center, Nijmegen, Netherlands.
   Abstract: Comprehensive survey covering CNN, RNN, and GAN approaches
   for medical image classification, segmentation, and registration.

2. Ronneberger O, Fischer P, Brox T. U-Net: Convolutional Networks for
   Biomedical Image Segmentation. In: MICCAI 2015. 2015;9351:234-241.
   DOI: 10.1007/978-3-319-24574-4_28.
   Institution: University of Freiburg, Freiburg, Germany.
   Abstract: Fully convolutional network with contracting encoder, symmetric
   decoder, and skip connections. Standard baseline for biomedical segmentation.

3. Oktay O, Schlemper J, Folgoc L, Lee M, Heinrich MP, Misawa K, Mori K,
   McDonagh S, Hammerla NY, Kainz B, Glocker B, Rueckert D. Attention U-Net:
   Learning Where to Look. arXiv. 2018. DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.1804.03999.
   Institution: University of Oxford, Oxford, UK.
   Abstract: Attention gates in U-Net skip connections suppress irrelevant
   regions. WT DSC 91.2% on BraTS 2018.

4. Milletari F, Navab N, Ahmadi SA. V-Net: Fully Convolutional Neural
   Networks for Volumetric Medical Image Segmentation. In: IEEE 3DV 2016.
   2016:565-571. DOI: 10.1109/3DV.2016.79.
   Institution: Technical University of Munich, Munich, Germany.
   Abstract: 3D CNN with residual blocks and dice loss. DSC improvements
   of 1-3% over 2D CNNs on BraTS.

5. He K, Zhang X, Ren S, Sun J. Deep Residual Learning for Image
   Recognition. In: IEEE CVPR 2016. 2016:770-778.
   DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.1512.03385.
   Institution: Microsoft Research, Redmond, WA, USA.
   Abstract: ResNet with residual skip connections. Foundational CNN
   architecture adapted to 3D for medical imaging.

6. Huang G, Liu Z, van der Maaten L, Weinberger KQ. Densely Connected
   Convolutional Networks. In: IEEE CVPR 2017. 2017:4700-4708.
   DOI: 10.48550/arXiv.1608.06993.
   Institution: Columbia University, New York, NY, USA.
   Abstract: DenseNet with dense skip connections. Efficient feature
   reuse with fewer parameters than ResNet.

7. Dosovitskiy A, Beyer L, Kolesnikov A, Weissenborn D, Zhai X,
